  "content": {
    "id": "p29-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Consider a class of 25 students. Assume that none are born in a leap year. Assume birthdays are independent and equally likely on each of the 365 days. Give probabilities to 2 decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What is the probability that all the members of the class have different birthdays?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.43$",
          "worked": "For each successive student, exclude the birthdays already used.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{all different})&=\\frac{365}{365}\\times\\frac{364}{365}\\times\\frac{363}{365}\\times\\cdots\\times\\frac{341}{365}\\\\P(\\text{all different})&=\\frac{365!}{340!\\,365^{25}}\\\\P(\\text{all different})&\\approx0.43\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What is the probability that two or more students share the same birthday? Comment.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.57$.\n\nA shared birthday is more likely than no shared birthday; this is the birthday paradox.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{shared birthday})&=1-P(\\text{all different})\\\\P(\\text{shared birthday})&=1-\\frac{365!}{340!\\,365^{25}}\\\\P(\\text{shared birthday})&\\approx0.57\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe probability exceeds $\\frac12$. There are $\\frac{25\\times24}{2}=300$ pairs of students who could share a birthday, explaining why a match is relatively likely.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 27
      }
    ]
  },
